===Birds nests===
{{Main|Birdhouse trapping}}

Birdhouse trapping on [[Fossil Island]] is a good source of [[tree seeds]] and [[fruit tree seeds]]. Birdhouses have a chance to drop a [[bird nest]], dependent on tier, which may contain seeds. Since they can be harvested every 50 minutes, the number of nests and seeds players harvest ends up being significant.

It's worth building the highest tier birdhouse possible, since the tier determines the number of nests harvested. The chance of receiving a seed nest however is not affected by birdhouse tier, only hunter level. <sup>[[Bird house trapping#Seed nest|[1]]]</sup>

===Slayer and bossing===
At lower levels, player can obtain seeds from different monsters while they are training [[Slayer]] or if in need, also off task. At middle and higher levels, players can obtain seeds consistently while they are on [[nechryael]] or [[dagannoth]] tasks. Nechryael in the [[Slayer Tower]] are an especially good task for herb seeds, as well as Prayer experience and coins.

Players can also get tree seeds from various bosses and demi-bosses, such as [[Zulrah]], [[lizardman shaman]]s, [[demonic gorilla]]s, [[Kalphite Queen]], [[Callisto]], and [[Venenatis]].

===Pickpocketing Master Farmers===
Players can start pickpocketing [[Master Farmer]]s at 38 Thieving to receive a variety of seeds.

[[Ironmen]] looking for herb seeds can expect up to 60 high level seeds ([[ranarr seeds]] or higher) per hour at maximum efficiency: 94 Thieving and the hard [[Ardougne Diary]] completed, where players stop failing pickpocketing [[Master Farmer]]s, or level 99 Thieving with the skillcape equipped.

===Wintertodt===
Ironmen can obtain a variety of seeds from the [[Wintertodt]] [[Reward Cart]]. The player’s related skill levels determine the rewards. A high Farming level increases the chance of getting higher level seeds, however they are still possible to obtain at 1 Farming.

==Obtaining compost==
[[Ultracompost]] can be made by buying [[pineapples]] from [[charter ship]]s or harvesting [[watermelon]]s, putting them into a [[compost bin]] and using 25 [[volcanic ash]]es (or 50 on the [[Big Compost Bin|big compost bin]] in the [[Farming Guild]]) on a full compost bin containing [[supercompost]]. Alternatively, with 22 [[Herblore]] one can make [[compost potion]] which will turn a regular compost bin into supercompost, and then use [[volcanic ash]]es for Ultracompost.

The [[Moons of Peril]] reward chest is an excellent source of supercompost which can also be converted using [[volcanic ash]]es for Ultracompost.

If using the [[Fertile Soil]] spell it is recommended that you unlock the enhanced version by obtaining the [[ash covered tome]] from the [[Volcanic Mine|volcanic mine]] [[Petrified Pete's Ore Shop|reward store]], as this negates the need to spend time making ultracompost.

